description: API layer, Axios usage, and service architecture standards
alwaysApply: false
---

# API Layer

Never place HTTP requests directly inside React components.

All API communication must live inside:
- services/
- api/
- lib/

---

# Axios Architecture

Centralize Axios configuration in:
- lib/api.js
- api/client.js

Avoid creating Axios instances inside individual service files.

---

# Services

Each service file should represent a domain.

Examples:
- moods.js
- comments.js
- users.js

Services should expose reusable async functions.

---

# Responsibilities

Services should:
- perform requests
- normalize responses
- normalize errors

Components should not know HTTP implementation details.

---

# Error Handling

Never throw raw Axios errors directly to UI.

Normalize API errors into predictable Error objects.

---

# Scalability

Assume backend endpoints may evolve.

Keep services loosely coupled from UI implementation.